>\nwith values in <MATH_0007>. Note that the diagram in <MATH_0008>\n<MATH_0009>\nis an equalizer diagram if and only if for every object <MATH_0010> of\n<MATH_0011> the diagram of sets\n<MATH_0012>\nis an equalizer diagram.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nSuppose <MATH_0013> is arbitrary.\nLet <MATH_0014> be a presheaf with values in <MATH_0015>.\nChoose any object <MATH_0016>.\nThen we get a presheaf of sets <MATH_0017> defined\nby the rule\n<MATH_0018>\nFrom the above it follows that a good definition is\nobtained by requiring all the presheaves <MATH_0019> to be\nsheaves of sets.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:988ab41a7259a45ab268fe7090009efd8135643a72ff205e7ba13845bfbccb84", "unit_id": "tag:00VL:prose-0003"}
